{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Maintainer decision (2026-08-17): RP-02 transaction semantics option A is APPROVED. RP-02 owns ordered exact-match retirement recovery at an explicit live-operation boundary: the durable tombstone is the retirement intent; recovery removes the live forward/reverse pair only when tombstone, forward, and reverse identities exactly agree; repeat is a no-op; ambiguity or replacement failure safety-aborts. Construction, ordinary load, and preview diagnose only and never write. This is an approved behavior delta from reloading the identity as simultaneously live and retired, not a claim of general multi-file or Jira/local ACID atomicity. RP-03 consumes the coherent post-recovery snapshot and owns TicketPlan orchestration/failure policy and post-create remote containment; it must not duplicate binding persistence recovery."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786998220453762001,"uuid":"f03c2909-e15f-4652-8fa8-f25db91e7586"}